  "id": "laryngeal-paralysis",
  "term": "laryngeal paralysis",
  "definition": "Laryngeal paralysis is a loss or marked reduction of normal movement in the larynx that can obstruct the upper airway. In the supplied source, it is identified by visually assessing laryngeal motion under light anesthesia, with more objective video-based measurement methods proposed to reduce observer disagreement.",
